1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,056
You!

2
00:00:01,056 --> 00:00:03,436
You're the man who's always in my dreams.

3
00:00:03,436 --> 00:00:05,071
You're telling me something.

4
00:00:05,071 --> 00:00:06,973
Protect my daughter.

5
00:00:06,973 --> 00:00:09,642
You might be going against
someone influential.

6
00:00:09,642 --> 00:00:11,811
And I don't want my daughter to get involved.

7
00:00:11,811 --> 00:00:14,781
I know that Sep's life was short.

8
00:00:14,781 --> 00:00:17,217
But many people love him.

9
00:00:17,217 --> 00:00:18,785
What do you mean by short life?

10
00:00:18,785 --> 00:00:20,854
- I don't understand you.
- Liam, what are you doing?

11
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:22,022
What do you mean?

12
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:24,290
Tell me, what's happening? Where's Sep?

13
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:25,291
Sep is dead.

14
00:00:25,291 --> 00:00:28,094
That night, we heard him screaming.

15
00:00:28,094 --> 00:00:31,431
When we went out,
we saw him on the ground unconscious.

16
00:00:31,431 --> 00:00:34,501
When we went to the gate,
it smelled like gasoline around the area.

17
00:00:34,501 --> 00:00:37,237
This office needs a new monster.

18
00:00:37,237 --> 00:00:39,372
- I'm your man.
- Make sure of it, Vergil.

19
00:00:39,372 --> 00:00:44,977
Because I'm not the type of man
who patiently waits to get what he wants.

20
00:00:58,927 --> 00:01:03,630
I don't get why Joyce
is making me fix her wedding.

21
00:01:04,265 --> 00:01:09,170
I might take care of their honeymoon, too.

22
00:01:09,170 --> 00:01:12,293
I'm sure Hans will be glad. Right, Hans?

23
00:01:14,008 --> 00:01:17,478
What's keeping you busy these days?

24
00:01:18,379 --> 00:01:21,249
To be fair to Joyce,

25
00:01:21,249 --> 00:01:23,685
she's also busy with the medical mission

26
00:01:23,685 --> 00:01:27,087
and renovation project
of the orphanage, right?

27
00:01:29,023 --> 00:01:33,895
Do we have vloggers and reporters there?

28
00:01:33,895 --> 00:01:35,096
It's a waste

29
00:01:35,096 --> 00:01:38,132
if there's no media coverage
to show my daughter's saintly deeds.

30
00:01:38,132 --> 00:01:39,700
Right?

31
00:01:40,561 --> 00:01:43,836
Anyway, let us proceed.

32
00:01:43,836 --> 00:01:47,639
I will show you the plan, okay?

33
00:01:50,244 --> 00:01:54,915
The theme... is water goddess realness.

34
00:01:57,251 --> 00:02:03,058
There will be overflowing water
in the vases outside the church.

35
00:02:03,058 --> 00:02:06,194
And there will be singing divas.
Five of them!

36
00:02:06,194 --> 00:02:08,630
Singing like mermaids.

37
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:11,266
They will sing at the wedding.

38
00:02:11,266 --> 00:02:12,867
And you know, it's going to be...

39
00:02:12,867 --> 00:02:14,902
Too much!

40
00:02:16,204 --> 00:02:19,207
Babe, did you approve this?

41
00:02:19,207 --> 00:02:23,110
I want it to be simple.
I told you that, right?

42
00:02:24,145 --> 00:02:25,946
Babe...

43
00:02:26,614 --> 00:02:30,452
Auntie's suggestion is fine.

44
00:02:30,452 --> 00:02:35,323
At least, our relationship has
been low-key before, right?

45
00:02:35,323 --> 00:02:39,661
Now, for once, I just want the whole world...

46
00:02:39,661 --> 00:02:42,163
And the universe, rather...

47
00:02:42,163 --> 00:02:44,002
To know you're mine.

48
00:02:45,934 --> 00:02:48,670
The universe, as Auntie said.

49
00:02:48,670 --> 00:02:51,172
Sir Hans, excuse me.

50
00:02:51,172 --> 00:02:55,343
Madam, I somehow agree with Miss Joyce.

51
00:02:55,343 --> 00:02:57,946
Isn't it too showy?

52
00:02:57,946 --> 00:03:01,649
It might take away
the solemnity of the ceremony.

53
00:03:03,852 --> 00:03:08,256
Why didn't you go to the meeting
if that's what you want?

54
00:03:08,256 --> 00:03:10,458
Why didn't you sit down with them?

55
00:03:10,458 --> 00:03:14,029
I've settled everything already,
and now you want to change the plan.

56
00:03:14,029 --> 00:03:16,263
I'm busy too.

57
00:03:17,032 --> 00:03:18,533
And you, Odet...

58
00:03:18,533 --> 00:03:20,368
if you want to take Joyce's side,

59
00:03:20,368 --> 00:03:23,404
you better walk her down the aisle too!

60
00:03:24,452 --> 00:03:29,577
Mommy, honestly, I'm just overwhelmed with...

61
00:03:31,379 --> 00:03:33,914
Babe, where?

62
00:03:35,717 --> 00:03:36,885
Expenses?

63
00:03:36,885 --> 00:03:38,485
Budget?

64
00:03:39,187 --> 00:03:40,821
Babe...

65
00:03:41,790 --> 00:03:45,526
I told you, I saved up for this
for a long time.

66
00:03:46,528 --> 00:03:49,330
This is for us. We deserve this.

67
00:03:50,732 --> 00:03:52,499
Babe.

68
00:03:54,702 --> 00:03:57,739
It's going to be
the wedding of the century!

69
00:03:57,739 --> 00:03:59,240
Imagine.

70
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:03,578
A big star will marry a hotshot lawyer

71
00:04:03,578 --> 00:04:06,081
who is also a promising politician.

72
00:04:06,081 --> 00:04:09,417
They really are a power couple!
Powerful, powerful!

73
00:04:09,417 --> 00:04:11,118
What can you say, babe?

74
00:04:11,986 --> 00:04:14,923
If that's what you want,
then I'm okay with it.

75
00:04:14,923 --> 00:04:16,391
Perfect!

76
00:04:16,391 --> 00:04:19,494
So now, I will show you...

77
00:04:19,494 --> 00:04:25,733
the gown with a super long train.

78
00:04:33,942 --> 00:04:36,010
Let's eat, love.

79
00:04:38,513 --> 00:04:41,916
Don't you want the food?
I can order pizza.

80
00:04:41,916 --> 00:04:44,351
No need. I'm okay with that.

81
00:04:47,388 --> 00:04:50,692
How's your project with Joyce
at the orphanage?

82
00:04:50,692 --> 00:04:52,527
You're lucky she has time for that...

83
00:04:52,527 --> 00:04:54,495
despite her busy schedule.

84
00:04:55,296 --> 00:04:56,864
We are doing okay.

85
00:04:57,899 --> 00:05:01,202
There is a lot to repair in the orphanage.

86
00:05:01,202 --> 00:05:05,439
The kids' living condition could be better.

87
00:05:08,643 --> 00:05:11,679
Love, do you want me to fix your schedule?

88
00:05:12,747 --> 00:05:15,382
I notice that you seem to...

89
00:05:15,984 --> 00:05:19,320
forget your promise to my father.

90
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,789
Didn't you say you'll help in his campaign?

91
00:05:21,789 --> 00:05:23,223
Via...

92
00:05:24,592 --> 00:05:25,660
Didn't I tell you

93
00:05:25,660 --> 00:05:28,429
that I'm having second thoughts
about that project?

94
00:05:29,631 --> 00:05:32,700
But you're not having second thoughts
about me, right?

95
00:05:36,237 --> 00:05:38,840
Laugh a little!

96
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:40,941
I'm joking.

97
00:05:41,743 --> 00:05:43,243
Sorry.

98
00:05:44,312 --> 00:05:45,713
It's fine.

99
00:05:46,347 --> 00:05:49,483
Dad's busy, too, with Casa Fuerte.

100
00:05:52,253 --> 00:05:55,956
I thought Congressman Ramon
had already let go of Casa Fuerte?

101
00:05:58,593 --> 00:06:02,030
He only let go of Uncle Danilo, remember?

102
00:06:02,030 --> 00:06:05,500
He's still hands-on
with your brother, Vergil.

103
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:07,635
You know what, love?

104
00:06:07,635 --> 00:06:09,704
You should hang out with him more

105
00:06:09,704 --> 00:06:12,974
instead of your showbiz friends.

106
00:06:12,974 --> 00:06:15,776
You will learn a lot from him.

107
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:21,449
Maybe you're right.

108
00:06:21,449 --> 00:06:23,851
There's a lot I need to learn.

109
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:35,063
I'm glad you came.

110
00:06:35,063 --> 00:06:41,769
It's only now that I enjoy my time
since I retired from work.

111
00:06:43,305 --> 00:06:45,340
Dad...

112
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:48,676
The truth is, I came here because...

113
00:06:48,676 --> 00:06:51,178
I want to know something about Casa Fuerte.

114
00:06:52,313 --> 00:06:55,849
You don't need to know anything
about Casa Fuerte.

115
00:06:56,651 --> 00:06:58,086
Business as usual.

116
00:06:58,086 --> 00:07:00,755
And I don't work there anymore.

117
00:07:00,755 --> 00:07:04,993
If you want to know something...
you can ask Vergil.

118
00:07:04,993 --> 00:07:06,627
He's on his way here.

119
00:07:07,695 --> 00:07:11,232
How can we be sure that
he'll tell me the truth?

120
00:07:11,232 --> 00:07:13,668
You know my brother.

121
00:07:13,668 --> 00:07:15,270
He's so...

122
00:07:15,270 --> 00:07:17,338
So...

123
00:07:17,338 --> 00:07:19,274
Intelligent?

124
00:07:19,274 --> 00:07:20,707
Great?

125
00:07:21,409 --> 00:07:24,044
I didn't know you admired me, Liam.

126
00:07:24,912 --> 00:07:26,781
You know what?

127
00:07:26,781 --> 00:07:32,486
I asked you to come here
to join me in my quiet time.

128
00:07:33,121 --> 00:07:37,692
But I think I made a mistake
inviting you both.

129
00:07:37,692 --> 00:07:41,228
Can we just have coffee?

130
00:07:42,630 --> 00:07:44,932
What does he want to know?

131
00:07:48,469 --> 00:07:52,040
What are your new projects in Casa Fuerte?

132
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:54,275
Why? Do you want to apply?

133
00:07:54,275 --> 00:07:56,411
Try talking to HR.

134
00:07:56,411 --> 00:08:00,380
What are your projects with Uncle Ramon?

135
00:08:01,215 --> 00:08:03,283
Why would I tell you?

136
00:08:04,252 --> 00:08:09,223
Now that I'm the CEO,
you can't order me around anymore.

137
00:08:09,223 --> 00:08:12,893
Also, you might end up getting jealous.

138
00:08:14,896 --> 00:08:17,397
An airport in the south.

139
00:08:18,166 --> 00:08:20,801
A big mall up north.

140
00:08:21,569 --> 00:08:26,473
And an old orphanage that will
become a condominium.

141
00:08:27,175 --> 00:08:28,809
You're surprised, right?

142
00:08:29,677 --> 00:08:32,045
What orphanage are you referring to?

143
00:08:32,847 --> 00:08:35,048
Ask Uncle Ramon about it.

144
00:08:40,455 --> 00:08:42,190
What?

145
00:08:42,190 --> 00:08:44,658
Are you scared to ask him?

146
00:08:46,594 --> 00:08:49,897
Because of all the wrong things
you did to his family?

147
00:08:52,033 --> 00:08:54,202
Tell me, Liam.

148
00:08:54,202 --> 00:08:55,670
Are you still cheating on Via?

149
00:08:55,670 --> 00:08:58,739
- Vergil, stop.
- Don't change the topic.

150
00:09:00,041 --> 00:09:02,110
Bahay Aruga.

151
00:09:02,110 --> 00:09:04,778
Uncle Ramon wants that property.

152
00:09:05,546 --> 00:09:07,315
There you go.

153
00:09:07,315 --> 00:09:08,782
I said it.

154
00:09:09,550 --> 00:09:11,619
You can now leave.

155
00:09:11,619 --> 00:09:15,022
Go wherever the hell you want
to do soul searching.

156
00:09:15,022 --> 00:09:17,558
I know you and Uncle Ramon.

157
00:09:17,558 --> 00:09:21,862
I know you'll try everything
just to get that property.

158
00:09:22,897 --> 00:09:24,866
Now, tell me.

159
00:09:24,866 --> 00:09:27,267
A kid died there.

160
00:09:28,503 --> 00:09:30,571
Do you have something to do with it?

161
00:09:30,571 --> 00:09:33,908
We heard him screaming that night.

162
00:09:33,908 --> 00:09:38,746
He sounded like he was fighting with someone.

163
00:09:38,746 --> 00:09:43,251
And when we went out,
we saw him on the ground, unconscious.

164
00:09:43,251 --> 00:09:45,253
Do you know what's puzzling?

165
00:09:45,253 --> 00:09:49,590
When we went to the gate,
the whole place smelled like gasoline.

166
00:09:49,590 --> 00:09:52,159
Liam, what are you talking about?

167
00:09:53,094 --> 00:09:54,995
What? Answer me.

168
00:09:57,398 --> 00:09:59,100
Dad...

169
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:01,702
are you just going to let your bastard child
disrespect me?

170
00:10:02,437 --> 00:10:05,606
Don't forget, I now have the highest position
in the company.

171
00:10:05,606 --> 00:10:07,575
Please!

172
00:10:07,575 --> 00:10:10,077
Stop, both of you!

173
00:10:10,077 --> 00:10:12,180
You, Liam.

174
00:10:12,180 --> 00:10:14,815
Be careful with your words.

175
00:10:16,117 --> 00:10:18,119
And you, Vergil.

176
00:10:18,119 --> 00:10:21,189
I want to know everything!

177
00:10:21,189 --> 00:10:24,358
All your dealings with Ramon.

178
00:10:25,126 --> 00:10:27,361
Ask your friend, then.

179
00:10:39,372 --> 00:10:41,442
[Medical Mission]

180
00:10:41,442 --> 00:10:43,311
Aren't you needed in your filming?

181
00:10:43,311 --> 00:10:46,247
We might be taking up too much of your time.

182
00:10:46,247 --> 00:10:47,748
Sister...

183
00:10:47,748 --> 00:10:51,219
I'm available any time for you.

184
00:10:51,219 --> 00:10:52,686
Thank you.

185
00:10:54,292 --> 00:10:55,822
Thank you.

186
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:07,234
You're early.

187
00:11:08,069 --> 00:11:11,005
I need to ask Sister something.

188
00:11:11,005 --> 00:11:12,939
What is it, son?

189
00:11:14,675 --> 00:11:16,577
Sister...

190
00:11:16,577 --> 00:11:18,679
Is anyone interested in this land

191
00:11:18,679 --> 00:11:21,415
where the orphanage is standing?

192
00:11:21,415 --> 00:11:24,018
How did you know?

193
00:11:24,018 --> 00:11:26,187
They're too pushy.

194
00:11:26,187 --> 00:11:29,256
I'm close to reporting them to the police.

195
00:11:30,324 --> 00:11:32,693
Is that Casa Fuerte?

196
00:11:32,693 --> 00:11:35,630
Yes, they insist on buying this land.

197
00:11:35,630 --> 00:11:40,468
I turned them down several times.
But they're so persistent.

198
00:11:40,468 --> 00:11:43,470
What will happen to the kids? Poor kids.

199
00:11:44,472 --> 00:11:48,942
I will never forget that name. Casa Fuerte.

200
00:11:53,976 --> 00:11:58,553
Sorry, Liam, I realized only now
that you're a Herrera.

201
00:11:58,553 --> 00:12:02,756
You own Casa Fuerte.

202
00:12:03,558 --> 00:12:11,399
Maybe you can ask your company
to stop trying to buy this land.

203
00:12:11,399 --> 00:12:13,967
I feel bad for the kids.

204
00:12:15,636 --> 00:12:18,573
Don't worry, Sister.

205
00:12:18,573 --> 00:12:21,375
Even though I'm no longer
part of Casa Fuerte,

206
00:12:21,375 --> 00:12:26,847
I will do everything I can
to prevent them from buying this property.

207
00:12:26,847 --> 00:12:28,082
Thank you.

208
00:12:28,082 --> 00:12:32,253
Now I'm hopeful that someone can help us.

209
00:12:32,253 --> 00:12:33,921
Excuse me.

210
00:12:33,921 --> 00:12:36,557
Sister, there's a call for you.

211
00:12:36,557 --> 00:12:40,694
Is that so?
I'll leave you for now. I'll be right back.

212
00:12:47,501 --> 00:12:49,002
Liam...

213
00:12:50,705 --> 00:12:54,875
Why is Casa Fuerte
interested in the orphanage?

214
00:12:56,110 --> 00:13:00,747
Actually, I just talked with Vergil.

215
00:13:01,749 --> 00:13:05,185
Honestly, I don't know
what Congressman Ramon's plans are.

216
00:13:07,421 --> 00:13:10,557
It's Congressman Ramon dela Peña again?

217
00:13:13,628 --> 00:13:16,096
What does he plan to do with this orphanage?

218
00:13:18,633 --> 00:13:22,702
We're late. They might get mad.

219
00:13:23,599 --> 00:13:25,666
Oh! Wait, baby.

220
00:13:29,810 --> 00:13:30,811
Hello!

221
00:13:30,811 --> 00:13:32,480
Sorry. Sorry, Sir.

222
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:36,716
Sorry, I'm late. I had to pick up Astig first.

223
00:13:38,119 --> 00:13:40,821
Hello, Astig.
I've been wanting to meet you.

224
00:13:40,821 --> 00:13:42,522
Hello.

225
00:13:43,557 --> 00:13:47,895
Sorry. I can't leave him with his dad.

226
00:13:47,895 --> 00:13:49,897
We had a fight last night.

227
00:13:49,897 --> 00:13:52,900
He didn't give financial support again.

228
00:13:52,900 --> 00:13:54,435
It's okay, Megan.

229
00:13:54,435 --> 00:13:56,303
It's okay.

230
00:13:56,303 --> 00:13:58,406
Are you sure, Sir?

231
00:13:58,406 --> 00:14:02,642
Looks like you're having a serious talk.

232
00:14:15,588 --> 00:14:18,826
My God. Here we go again.

233
00:14:18,826 --> 00:14:22,983
I thought we already hit rock bottom
when we stayed in the movie

234
00:14:22,983 --> 00:14:26,667
just so you can be with Liam.

235
00:14:26,667 --> 00:14:28,502
I didn't know it could get worse.

236
00:14:28,502 --> 00:14:32,306
- This is desperation...
- Sister, these are vitamins.

237
00:14:32,306 --> 00:14:34,308
You can give it to the kids.

238
00:14:34,308 --> 00:14:36,310
There's vitamin C...

239
00:14:36,310 --> 00:14:37,378
- An orphanage?
- To prevent them from viruses.

240
00:14:37,378 --> 00:14:39,280
Love!

241
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:40,506
Hi.

242
00:14:40,506 --> 00:14:42,236
I brought some clothes.

243
00:14:42,982 --> 00:14:46,275
My celebrity and model friends

244
00:14:46,275 --> 00:14:48,956
heard about your project for the orphans.

245
00:14:48,956 --> 00:14:51,024
So they sent some clothes.

246
00:14:52,059 --> 00:14:54,228
There, perfect. Hey, Odet.

247
00:14:54,228 --> 00:14:57,131
Instead of just standing there,
why don't you help me instead.

248
00:14:57,131 --> 00:14:58,532
Odet!

249
00:14:59,366 --> 00:15:01,335
Excuse me?

250
00:15:01,335 --> 00:15:02,970
I have a role to play here.

251
00:15:02,970 --> 00:15:04,672
How about you? What's your part?

252
00:15:04,672 --> 00:15:06,807
Just because you are
wearing heavier makeup

253
00:15:06,807 --> 00:15:07,908
doesn't make you better than me.

254
00:15:07,908 --> 00:15:09,342
We're both assistants.

255
00:15:09,342 --> 00:15:12,345
And with your arms,
you can definitely handle that job!

256
00:15:13,814 --> 00:15:18,618
And you have hideous feet.
Keep away those eyesores!

257
00:15:19,553 --> 00:15:22,022
- What?
- At least it's just my feet.

258
00:15:22,022 --> 00:15:23,991
You look hideous all over!

259
00:15:23,991 --> 00:15:25,358
Hey!

260
00:15:26,043 --> 00:15:27,995
Ma'am, stop me.

261
00:15:27,995 --> 00:15:29,597
Girl, let's go.

262
00:15:29,597 --> 00:15:31,866
Are you going somewhere, Joyce?

263
00:15:31,866 --> 00:15:34,068
Are you leaving because I came?

264
00:15:34,068 --> 00:15:36,203
It's not like that, Via.

265
00:15:36,203 --> 00:15:38,739
I need to take care of something.

266
00:15:38,739 --> 00:15:42,075
I have to meet Hans.

267
00:15:43,043 --> 00:15:45,579
Liam, is it okay if I go ahead?

268
00:15:45,579 --> 00:15:48,248
I told Megan everything
that needs to be done.

269
00:15:51,285 --> 00:15:52,819
Love?

270
00:15:53,721 --> 00:15:56,990
Joyce is asking if she can leave.

271
00:15:58,092 --> 00:15:59,460
Yes.

272
00:15:59,460 --> 00:16:01,561
Be safe.

273
00:16:05,299 --> 00:16:06,967
Sorry, Via.

274
00:16:06,967 --> 00:16:09,637
I have a prior commitment.

275
00:16:09,637 --> 00:16:11,939
Don't be sorry.

276
00:16:11,939 --> 00:16:16,843
We really should value our commitments.

277
00:16:18,813 --> 00:16:20,447
Bye.

278
00:16:34,061 --> 00:16:37,498
Don't tell me I can't stay here, too.

279
00:16:37,498 --> 00:16:39,966
This is for the kids.

280
00:16:44,338 --> 00:16:46,773
Give Sister the clothes.

281
00:16:47,508 --> 00:16:49,343
Sister?

282
00:16:49,343 --> 00:16:52,813
Here are branded clothes for the kids.

283
00:16:52,813 --> 00:16:56,983
Those with broken hearts
can also use it to wipe their tears.

284
00:17:05,893 --> 00:17:08,629
Chef, thank you so much for your time.

285
00:17:08,629 --> 00:17:12,199
I'm glad Hans tapped you for our wedding.

286
00:17:12,199 --> 00:17:14,101
I can't say no to Hans.

287
00:17:14,101 --> 00:17:16,937
And I'm super honored
that you picked me for your special day.

288
00:17:16,937 --> 00:17:21,408
I don't often cook for celebrities like you.

289
00:17:21,408 --> 00:17:23,944
Oh, come on, Chef.

290
00:17:23,944 --> 00:17:25,813
You're a celebrity, too.

291
00:17:25,813 --> 00:17:27,982
- That's right.
- You're more famous, Joyce.

292
00:17:27,982 --> 00:17:31,285
I bumped into you on the set
of a morning show.

293
00:17:31,285 --> 00:17:34,787
I wanted to take a picture with you,
but I felt shy.

294
00:17:34,787 --> 00:17:37,258
You don't have to be shy now, Chef.

295
00:17:37,258 --> 00:17:39,460
You can ask my wife
to make video greetings.

296
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:41,629
You can ask for three or four.

297
00:17:41,629 --> 00:17:43,130
That's embarrassing, babe.

298
00:17:43,130 --> 00:17:44,565
I'd love that, bro.

299
00:17:44,565 --> 00:17:48,302
Actually, my friends are
big fans of all your hit movies.

300
00:17:48,302 --> 00:17:49,770
And because of that,

301
00:17:49,770 --> 00:17:52,907
I'll be preparing my go-to
and favorite dishes

302
00:17:52,907 --> 00:17:54,642
for your wedding reception.

303
00:17:54,642 --> 00:17:56,076
- It will be a blockbuster too.
- That's a blockbuster.

304
00:17:56,076 --> 00:17:59,647
And here's my menu proposal.

305
00:17:59,647 --> 00:18:01,214
Let's see.

306
00:18:06,987 --> 00:18:09,323
Wait. Comfort food?

307
00:18:09,323 --> 00:18:12,960
Isn't this too fatty, Chef?

308
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:15,996
Not necessarily for the super healthy people.

309
00:18:15,996 --> 00:18:19,133
But my menu will really indulge you.

310
00:18:19,133 --> 00:18:21,869
It will be so delicious,
and I promise you, guys,

311
00:18:21,869 --> 00:18:23,570
it won't let you down.

312
00:18:24,271 --> 00:18:26,840
You said so yourself.

313
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:28,675
Just once.

314
00:18:30,678 --> 00:18:34,448
Wait. Don't we have other choices?

315
00:18:34,448 --> 00:18:37,318
Can we talk about it first?

316
00:18:37,318 --> 00:18:39,520
Sure, Mr. and Mrs. Arevalo.

317
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:41,188
I'll leave you for now.

318
00:18:41,188 --> 00:18:43,490
But I'll ask for a video greeting later.

319
00:18:50,798 --> 00:18:52,299
Babe?

320
00:18:52,299 --> 00:18:57,470
Don't you think Aunt Joanne will get mad
if we have that at our wedding?

321
00:18:59,006 --> 00:19:00,407
You and my mom

322
00:19:00,407 --> 00:19:04,678
almost decided on everything
regarding our wedding.

323
00:19:04,678 --> 00:19:07,647
Is it okay if I decide on the food?

324
00:19:10,851 --> 00:19:13,721
Babe, sorry, but...

325
00:19:13,721 --> 00:19:16,190
I'm just thinking about your endorsements...

326
00:19:16,190 --> 00:19:19,526
Especially the organic food space.
Don't you think it's too...

327
00:19:19,526 --> 00:19:21,929
This menu, it's a bit out of your...

328
00:19:21,929 --> 00:19:24,497
Why do you talk like my mom?

329
00:19:28,235 --> 00:19:31,905
Babe, I'm just concerned about
your image as a celebrity.

330
00:19:31,905 --> 00:19:34,307
Hans, I'm the one you're going to marry,

331
00:19:35,209 --> 00:19:37,177
not my image.

332
00:19:44,685 --> 00:19:47,521
Miss Via, thank you for the clothes.
[Bahay Aruga Orphanage]

333
00:19:47,521 --> 00:19:50,590
Anytime, Sister. You're welcome.

334
00:19:53,227 --> 00:19:54,795
Excuse me, Sister.

335
00:19:54,795 --> 00:19:57,564
Excuse me, Sir.

336
00:19:57,564 --> 00:19:59,933
What are you doing here?

337
00:19:59,933 --> 00:20:02,069
Uncle Ramon told me to come here.

338
00:20:02,069 --> 00:20:04,103
Our future Senator.

339
00:20:05,806 --> 00:20:09,542
So it's true that you're having
the orphanage renovated.

340
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:13,614
Keep the orphanage out of your dirty job.

341
00:20:13,614 --> 00:20:17,251
So this is why you don't have time
for Uncle Ramon's campaign.

342
00:20:17,251 --> 00:20:20,019
You're wasting your time on this nonsense.

343
00:20:20,721 --> 00:20:24,491
I'm glad you're the ones here,
and not the other woman...

344
00:20:24,491 --> 00:20:25,892
Vergil.

345
00:20:35,102 --> 00:20:37,504
- Hey, Hans!
- Judge Policarpio.

346
00:20:37,504 --> 00:20:39,773
Good day. This is Joyce.

347
00:20:39,773 --> 00:20:41,508
I'm glad I saw you.

348
00:20:41,508 --> 00:20:43,343
I couldn't contact you.

349
00:20:43,343 --> 00:20:45,778
Perfect timing, you're with Joyce.

350
00:20:46,613 --> 00:20:48,148
Hello.

351
00:20:48,148 --> 00:20:49,917
I'm Reggie Policarpio.

352
00:20:49,917 --> 00:20:52,753
Yes, Judge. I know you.

353
00:20:52,753 --> 00:20:57,257
I just want to ask you about my movie offer.

354
00:20:59,293 --> 00:21:03,297
I want to produce a movie.
And I told Hans about it.

355
00:21:03,297 --> 00:21:06,166
This is about one of the cases I handled.

356
00:21:06,166 --> 00:21:11,538
It's about an abused mom
who fought for her kids' custody.

357
00:21:11,538 --> 00:21:14,297
The story is very inspiring.

358
00:21:16,944 --> 00:21:20,313
Hans? Looks like you haven't told Joyce yet.

359
00:21:24,718 --> 00:21:27,154
Sorry, Judge.

360
00:21:27,154 --> 00:21:29,556
I forgot about it.

361
00:21:29,556 --> 00:21:32,959
We're busy taking care of our wedding.

362
00:21:33,627 --> 00:21:35,829
No worries. I understand.

363
00:21:35,829 --> 00:21:38,165
Sorry, I forgot you're getting married.

364
00:21:38,165 --> 00:21:41,034
Maybe we're just going
to get another actress.

365
00:21:41,702 --> 00:21:45,706
We can hear your pitch, Judge.

366
00:21:45,706 --> 00:21:48,075
I will have my mom talk to you.

367
00:21:48,075 --> 00:21:50,677
Sure. With Ma'am Joanne?

368
00:21:52,579 --> 00:21:54,515
Thanks for considering.

369
00:21:54,515 --> 00:21:57,184
We can really see you for the role.

370
00:21:57,184 --> 00:21:59,319
We'll wait for your call.

371
00:22:01,688 --> 00:22:03,557
Thank you so much.

372
00:22:03,557 --> 00:22:05,325
Be safe, Judge.

373
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:07,560
I'll go ahead.

374
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:15,401
Did you forget to tell me?

375
00:22:18,968 --> 00:22:22,104
Or you purposely tried to block
a potential project?

376
00:22:28,182 --> 00:22:30,383
Sorry, Joyce.

377
00:22:32,085 --> 00:22:34,888
For seven years,
I've been sharing you with the world.

378
00:22:34,888 --> 00:22:36,723
I just thought...

379
00:22:36,723 --> 00:22:40,593
maybe there's a chance
I could have you only for myself.

380
00:22:42,529 --> 00:22:45,431
Hans, this is me, and this is what I do.

381
00:22:47,401 --> 00:22:50,925
You loved me as I am.

382
00:22:51,738 --> 00:22:53,240
Joyce, no.

383
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:57,411
You know how big a deal it is for me
when people control my life.

384
00:22:57,411 --> 00:22:59,313
You know that.

385
00:22:59,313 --> 00:23:00,781
No. It's not that...

386
00:23:00,781 --> 00:23:02,882
What if we're already married?

387
00:23:07,287 --> 00:23:12,503
What other decisions will you make
without me knowing?

388
00:23:17,397 --> 00:23:19,365
Joyce, it's not...

389
00:23:21,735 --> 00:23:23,036
Joyce.

390
00:23:27,608 --> 00:23:30,310
I won't waste your time, Sister.

391
00:23:30,310 --> 00:23:34,914
Looks like you're busy
and will probably do your novena later.

392
00:23:38,452 --> 00:23:41,287
How much money are we talking about here?

393
00:23:42,374 --> 00:23:44,591
Name your price.

394
00:23:44,591 --> 00:23:47,494
This will be a big help for the kids.

395
00:23:47,494 --> 00:23:52,098
The Congressman can pay
for what you need.

396
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:55,168
I thought...

397
00:23:55,168 --> 00:24:00,339
you understood that we're not interested
in selling this land.

398
00:24:02,226 --> 00:24:07,848
If the land is your concern,
we have lots of it.

399
00:24:07,848 --> 00:24:11,018
More spacious and way better.

400
00:24:11,018 --> 00:24:12,986
We have lands overlooking the city.

401
00:24:12,986 --> 00:24:15,522
We have properties near the beach.

402
00:24:15,522 --> 00:24:19,792
Sister, kids love the beach.

403
00:24:20,527 --> 00:24:24,831
I know why you're Interested in this land.

404
00:24:24,831 --> 00:24:31,171
What will the kids say
if they learn they were kicked out

405
00:24:31,171 --> 00:24:34,174
because you want to convert their house
into a gambling den?

406
00:24:34,174 --> 00:24:36,710
Forgive me. I'm sorry, son.

407
00:24:36,710 --> 00:24:39,346
I disagree with your plan.

408
00:24:39,346 --> 00:24:41,048
Sorry, Sir.

409
00:24:41,048 --> 00:24:43,917
But I have a background in Psychology.

410
00:24:43,917 --> 00:24:48,088
We take care of kids
who experienced severe trauma.

411
00:24:48,088 --> 00:24:52,992
It's not good for them
if we move them to another place.

412
00:24:55,762 --> 00:24:57,063
Vergil...

413
00:24:58,865 --> 00:25:03,836
Can you stop being a puppet
to grow dirty money?

414
00:25:04,871 --> 00:25:07,874
We were given a chance to change.

415
00:25:07,874 --> 00:25:10,043
But what did you choose?

416
00:25:10,043 --> 00:25:13,213
You chose to be greedy.

417
00:25:13,213 --> 00:25:17,784
I dreamt of something.
It's like an alternate reality.

418
00:25:17,784 --> 00:25:19,919
And in that dream...

419
00:25:20,587 --> 00:25:23,223
I saw how you rot in jail.

420
00:25:23,223 --> 00:25:25,425
Don't test my patience, Liam!

421
00:25:25,425 --> 00:25:28,195
If you try to bring me down,
I will take you with me.

422
00:25:28,195 --> 00:25:30,063
I don't care if Dad gets involved.

423
00:25:30,063 --> 00:25:32,632
- We'll all end up in jail.
- Keep Dad out of this.

424
00:25:32,632 --> 00:25:34,601
I'm warning you.

425
00:25:34,601 --> 00:25:37,537
You're playing the good son again, huh?

426
00:25:37,537 --> 00:25:39,740
Go and be with Dad!

427
00:25:39,740 --> 00:25:42,743
You're both like dogs
whose tails have been cut off.

428
00:25:42,743 --> 00:25:44,411
That's enough.

429
00:25:44,411 --> 00:25:46,079
Stop. That's enough.

430
00:25:46,079 --> 00:25:49,282
Please stop. I'm begging you.
That's enough.

431
00:25:52,119 --> 00:25:54,321
Stop threatening us.

432
00:25:54,321 --> 00:25:56,623
We're having a medical mission

433
00:25:56,623 --> 00:26:00,060
because a kid died of sickness.

434
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:01,895
His name is Sep.

435
00:26:01,895 --> 00:26:04,431
The kids are just starting to recover

436
00:26:04,431 --> 00:26:09,469
and be hopeful that they won't
end up like Sep,

437
00:26:09,469 --> 00:26:12,738
who died because we had no money
for his medication.

438
00:26:13,907 --> 00:26:16,109
Sister, I'm sorry.

439
00:26:16,109 --> 00:26:20,914
It looks like my brother already
sold his soul to the devil.

440
00:26:20,914 --> 00:26:22,349
Oh, really?

441
00:26:23,450 --> 00:26:24,618
- Stop!
- Hey!

442
00:26:24,618 --> 00:26:26,044
Come on!

443
00:26:26,987 --> 00:26:28,422
Stop it!

444
00:26:28,422 --> 00:26:29,623
Go ahead!

445
00:26:29,623 --> 00:26:30,924
- Go and try to do something! You!
- Don't!

446
00:26:30,924 --> 00:26:33,360
- Stop!
- You! Move there!

447
00:26:33,360 --> 00:26:36,296
Please stop. My God. Merciful heaven.

448
00:26:36,296 --> 00:26:37,364
Please stop.

449
00:26:37,364 --> 00:26:39,098
Try me, Liam!

450
00:26:40,634 --> 00:26:42,836
I didn't want to use violence.

451
00:26:42,836 --> 00:26:45,504
But you're testing my patience!

452
00:26:46,273 --> 00:26:47,807
You, Liam.

453
00:26:48,442 --> 00:26:49,509
You know what happens to those

454
00:26:49,509 --> 00:26:52,244
who get in the way
of the Congressman's plans.

455
00:26:52,244 --> 00:26:54,413
Does Papa know about that, Vergil?

456
00:26:54,413 --> 00:26:57,149
Stop making a scene here!

457
00:26:57,149 --> 00:26:58,491
We know we're just ordinary people.

458
00:26:58,491 --> 00:27:02,087
We're not at your level.
But please don't harass us.

459
00:27:02,087 --> 00:27:04,623
Please think of the children's welfare.

460
00:27:04,623 --> 00:27:07,975
Just because you'll give money
and offer another land

461
00:27:07,975 --> 00:27:11,597
doesn't mean the kids will accept it.

462
00:27:11,597 --> 00:27:15,133
Our life is simple. But we are happy.

463
00:27:18,137 --> 00:27:21,473
Please, leave us alone.

464
00:27:22,174 --> 00:27:24,409
Vergil Herrera!

465
00:27:25,611 --> 00:27:27,245
Stop what you're doing.

466
00:27:34,787 --> 00:27:38,123
Do you do that to scare people?

467
00:27:39,124 --> 00:27:41,760
Why don't you try me?

468
00:27:41,760 --> 00:27:45,764
Let's see what happens
to the congressman you idolize

469
00:27:45,764 --> 00:27:49,134
once I speak up about what you did here.

470
00:27:59,311 --> 00:28:01,179
We're not done yet.

471
00:28:18,731 --> 00:28:20,231
Are you okay?

472
00:28:20,231 --> 00:28:21,732
I'm okay.

473
00:28:23,770 --> 00:28:26,172
Do you have ice?

474
00:28:26,172 --> 00:28:29,141
Sister... are you okay?

475
00:28:30,100 --> 00:28:32,284
[Bahay Aruga Orphanage]

476
00:28:54,067 --> 00:28:56,502
Joyce, I'm sorry about earlier.

477
00:29:04,143 --> 00:29:07,012
I just had a hard time trying to...

478
00:29:07,714 --> 00:29:10,115
to have control.

479
00:29:12,685 --> 00:29:15,621
Isn't that how life is?

480
00:29:21,060 --> 00:29:24,163
We don't have control over everything.

481
00:29:29,170 --> 00:29:31,705
Maybe we really are alike.

482
00:29:32,639 --> 00:29:34,506
As for me...

483
00:29:35,375 --> 00:29:38,343
I have so many "what ifs".

484
00:29:41,180 --> 00:29:43,449
What is Liam Herrera's...

485
00:29:44,984 --> 00:29:47,386
"what if"?

486
00:29:54,927 --> 00:29:56,728
What if...

487
00:29:58,398 --> 00:30:05,204
I did not make
the big mistake I did before...

488
00:30:07,607 --> 00:30:14,046
in my attempt to make everything right?

489
00:30:16,916 --> 00:30:18,750
I did not know that...

490
00:30:21,554 --> 00:30:27,693
I would lose the people who love me.

491
00:30:31,130 --> 00:30:32,598
How about you?

492
00:30:33,433 --> 00:30:35,567
What are your "what ifs"?

493
00:30:45,578 --> 00:30:47,546
What if...

494
00:30:48,508 --> 00:30:51,543
I dared to take a risk?

495
00:30:56,155 --> 00:30:57,923
What if...

496
00:31:02,135 --> 00:31:05,838
What if Sep is still with us?

497
00:31:07,800 --> 00:31:12,104
What if there is a way to change the past?

498
00:31:27,521 --> 00:31:28,955
Let's go.

499
00:31:28,955 --> 00:31:30,923
Sister might already be looking for us.

500
00:31:30,923 --> 00:31:32,424
Joyce...

501
00:32:26,110 --> 00:32:28,648
I'm sorry.

502
00:32:28,648 --> 00:32:30,515
I'm sorry, Joyce.

503
00:32:38,891 --> 00:32:42,995
Liam, we just talked about wrong decisions.

504
00:32:45,765 --> 00:32:48,200
Let's choose what's right.

505
00:33:02,415 --> 00:33:03,749
<i>Hello, friends!</i>
[Girl With Periwinkle Hair]

506
00:33:03,749 --> 00:33:07,753
<i>It's me again,
your trusted showbiz authority.</i>

507
00:33:07,753 --> 00:33:11,390
<i>The Girl with the Periwinkle Hair!</i>

508
00:33:11,390 --> 00:33:17,263
<i>I'm not sure what kind of love boat
Joycelyn Trinidad is in.</i>

509
00:33:17,263 --> 00:33:20,766
<i>Some of you might say that I have no basis.</i>

510
00:33:20,766 --> 00:33:24,236
<i>Well, see it for yourselves.</i>

511
00:33:31,645 --> 00:33:38,084
Do you know how it will affect my campaign?

512
00:33:41,120 --> 00:33:47,259
Now, I have to act,
so they won't call me a bad father.

513
00:33:47,994 --> 00:33:53,432
I have warned you a long time ago
about those snakes.

514
00:33:57,923 --> 00:34:00,025
Then don't, Dad.

515
00:34:01,440 --> 00:34:03,875
Don't protect me...

516
00:34:04,810 --> 00:34:09,981
if you're only worried about
your campaign as a senator.

517
00:34:11,651 --> 00:34:14,020
Haven't you thought about it?

518
00:34:14,020 --> 00:34:19,391
Your only child has been
cheated on by her boyfriend!

519
00:34:25,498 --> 00:34:26,798
Via.

520
00:34:27,533 --> 00:34:28,834
Via!

521
00:34:28,834 --> 00:34:30,602
Come back here!

522
00:34:40,546 --> 00:34:43,049
We can deny it.

523
00:34:43,049 --> 00:34:45,718
We can say that it's just
someone who looks like Joyce.

524
00:34:45,718 --> 00:34:46,852
Right?

525
00:34:46,852 --> 00:34:50,022
Or there's someone who wants to ruin her.

526
00:34:50,022 --> 00:34:50,856
- Right?
- We can use that.

527
00:34:50,856 --> 00:34:52,692
Or say that the picture was edited.

528
00:34:52,692 --> 00:34:55,994
Let's release edited photos.

529
00:34:56,896 --> 00:34:59,031
Or let's make it look like
it's taken from a bad angle.

530
00:34:59,031 --> 00:35:00,670
- Yes.
- Liam could just be

531
00:35:00,670 --> 00:35:02,301
whispering something to her.

532
00:35:02,301 --> 00:35:03,869
But the angle made it
look like they were kissing.

533
00:35:03,869 --> 00:35:05,838
- We can do that, right?
- Let's try it.

534
00:35:05,838 --> 00:35:07,540
- Perfect.
- Odet, take a picture of us.

535
00:35:07,540 --> 00:35:09,342
Wait, wait. Hold on.

536
00:35:09,342 --> 00:35:13,412
Can we please... not worry about it for now?

537
00:35:13,412 --> 00:35:17,049
Everyone's talking about
our daughter's private life.

538
00:35:17,049 --> 00:35:21,520
There are many speculations
and judgments about her.

539
00:35:21,520 --> 00:35:22,655
And what do you want to do?

540
00:35:22,655 --> 00:35:26,692
You want to make it look like it's fake news?

541
00:35:26,692 --> 00:35:29,661
Dad, let them be.

542
00:35:29,661 --> 00:35:32,164
You should really let us be.

543
00:35:32,164 --> 00:35:38,725
Because no one cleans up your mess but me.

544
00:35:38,725 --> 00:35:41,440
And now you're going to tolerate her?

545
00:35:41,440 --> 00:35:43,776
There would have been nothing to clean up

546
00:35:43,776 --> 00:35:46,545
if only your daughter
didn't flirt with another guy.

547
00:36:38,129 --> 00:36:40,566
[Bahay Aruga Orphanage]

548
00:36:40,566 --> 00:36:44,770
Liam, we don't want to interfere

549
00:36:44,770 --> 00:36:49,008
with whatever relationship
you and Joyce have.

550
00:36:49,008 --> 00:36:51,164
- But...
- But,

551
00:36:51,164 --> 00:36:54,647
Miss Joyce is a famous celebrity.

552
00:36:54,647 --> 00:36:56,682
The orphanage is getting
dragged into the issue.

553
00:36:56,682 --> 00:36:59,518
They say that we're covering up
your affair...

554
00:36:59,518 --> 00:37:01,253
That we're tolerating you...

555
00:37:01,253 --> 00:37:05,157
And that you turned the orphanage
into your rendezvous.

556
00:37:05,157 --> 00:37:08,661
The medical mission you organized
for the kids is a really big help.

557
00:37:08,661 --> 00:37:13,666
But we're also facing
a serious issue right now.

558
00:37:13,666 --> 00:37:16,435
I understand, Lerna.

559
00:37:16,435 --> 00:37:17,936
Sister...

560
00:37:18,704 --> 00:37:20,305
Arnel.

561
00:37:50,002 --> 00:37:52,671
What's going on between you and Liam?

562
00:37:52,671 --> 00:37:55,040
We were just talking.

563
00:37:58,911 --> 00:38:02,213
We became emotional.

564
00:38:09,188 --> 00:38:12,190
Was it about our fight the other day?

565
00:38:32,411 --> 00:38:33,912
Joyce?

566
00:38:36,081 --> 00:38:37,582
Joyce?

567
00:38:44,023 --> 00:38:46,057
Don't you like me anymore?

568
00:38:54,099 --> 00:38:56,569
Nothing's going on between Liam and me.

569
00:38:56,569 --> 00:38:59,586
See? You're not answering my question.

570
00:39:01,740 --> 00:39:04,509
I'm asking you if you don't like me anymore.

571
00:39:10,583 --> 00:39:12,417
Hans...

572
00:39:15,955 --> 00:39:18,423
I've waited for you for seven years.

573
00:39:19,391 --> 00:39:21,092
Seven years.

574
00:39:26,165 --> 00:39:27,766
And then suddenly...

575
00:39:30,302 --> 00:39:32,071
that.

576
00:39:32,071 --> 00:39:35,140
You've known Liam for a short while,

577
00:39:35,140 --> 00:39:36,908
but it seems like...

578
00:39:38,310 --> 00:39:42,147
you've known each other better than we do.

579
00:39:42,147 --> 00:39:44,949
That's how I feel, Joyce. Want to know why?

580
00:39:46,986 --> 00:39:48,953
Whenever I look at you...

581
00:39:50,756 --> 00:39:54,492
Whenever I see the way you look at him...

582
00:39:57,096 --> 00:40:00,298
Whenever you're together,
I see how happy you are.

583
00:40:04,103 --> 00:40:06,137
I know, Joyce.

584
00:40:07,339 --> 00:40:10,642
I know because
you used to look at me that way.

585
00:40:36,368 --> 00:40:38,470
That's enough.

586
00:40:40,476 --> 00:40:42,767
Auntie, where did I go wrong?

587
00:40:43,876 --> 00:40:45,877
Via...

588
00:40:55,888 --> 00:40:57,423
That's enough, my dear.

589
00:40:57,423 --> 00:40:59,046
That's enough.

590
00:41:05,397 --> 00:41:07,433
Son, you two should talk.

591
00:41:07,433 --> 00:41:09,868
Talk to Via.

592
00:41:18,711 --> 00:41:21,246
Liam, let's make this work.

593
00:41:24,083 --> 00:41:27,152
Maybe it's good that this happened...

594
00:41:29,455 --> 00:41:34,592
So I will stop wondering
what's wrong with us.

595
00:41:37,730 --> 00:41:39,864
And that's Joyce.

596
00:41:44,069 --> 00:41:45,771
Love...

597
00:41:45,771 --> 00:41:49,274
Love, we can still solve this.

598
00:41:49,274 --> 00:41:54,012
Via, what are you saying?
How do we solve this?

599
00:42:00,819 --> 00:42:02,454
Please, choose me.

600
00:42:02,454 --> 00:42:04,088
Please.

601
00:42:04,790 --> 00:42:06,758
Love, please?

602
00:42:07,993 --> 00:42:09,761
Please.

603
00:42:10,629 --> 00:42:12,931
Choose me.

604
00:42:16,502 --> 00:42:18,670
Via, I'm sorry.

605
00:42:18,670 --> 00:42:19,972
No.

606
00:42:19,972 --> 00:42:21,306
No.

607
00:42:22,694 --> 00:42:24,910
Why are you sorry?

608
00:42:24,910 --> 00:42:27,212
Because you love somebody else?

609
00:42:28,551 --> 00:42:31,720
Because you cannot choose me?

610
00:42:34,119 --> 00:42:35,774
Love...

611
00:42:37,189 --> 00:42:41,292
Are you really going to throw away
the seven years we had?

612
00:42:42,261 --> 00:42:44,596
For that bitch!

613
00:42:44,596 --> 00:42:47,166
Please, please, please.

614
00:42:47,166 --> 00:42:48,534
Don't do this, please.

615
00:42:48,534 --> 00:42:50,135
- Here I am. This is me.
- Via, Via.

616
00:42:50,135 --> 00:42:51,537
- Via...
- It's me.

617
00:42:51,537 --> 00:42:54,505
Via, I'm sorry.

618
00:42:58,844 --> 00:43:00,478
I'm sorry.

619
00:43:24,403 --> 00:43:26,871
I'm sorry too, Liam.

620
00:43:28,540 --> 00:43:32,010
I don't know what can happen
because of your decision.

621
00:43:32,811 --> 00:43:34,145
Via!

622
00:43:36,148 --> 00:43:37,409
Via...

623
00:43:38,217 --> 00:43:40,018
Via, please.

624
00:43:40,819 --> 00:43:43,454
Don't do anything stupid.

625
00:43:49,194 --> 00:43:50,695
Via...

626
00:43:54,099 --> 00:43:58,070
I'm the reason. I'm the reason Joyce died.

627
00:43:58,070 --> 00:44:01,406
Please, forgive me. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

628
00:44:01,406 --> 00:44:03,108
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

629
00:44:03,108 --> 00:44:04,895
Hey!

630
00:44:11,250 --> 00:44:13,384
You're the one I love.

631
00:44:16,021 --> 00:44:17,889
Really, Love?

632
00:44:20,259 --> 00:44:23,695
Yes, Love.

633
00:44:37,409 --> 00:44:40,979
Joyce, thousands of fans are watching.

634
00:44:40,979 --> 00:44:43,414
What do you want to tell them?

635
00:44:49,721 --> 00:44:51,923
I want to say sorry...

636
00:44:53,926 --> 00:44:56,761
to those who got disappointed.

637
00:44:59,631 --> 00:45:03,969
I want to apologize to the people
who got affected by what I did.

638
00:45:03,969 --> 00:45:05,355
Because of what happened,

639
00:45:05,355 --> 00:45:08,974
I realized that it's so hard to live
under the watchful eyes of everyone.

640
00:45:08,974 --> 00:45:12,944
I realized it's hard to live having to...

641
00:45:14,446 --> 00:45:19,818
explain everything I do
because of malicious news.

642
00:45:19,818 --> 00:45:23,788
So now, I have come to a decision.

643
00:45:27,292 --> 00:45:29,961
I'll take a break from showbiz.

644
00:45:30,963 --> 00:45:32,497
Cut!

645
00:45:34,099 --> 00:45:36,802
What do you mean by "taking a break"?

646
00:45:36,802 --> 00:45:38,270
What?

647
00:45:38,270 --> 00:45:41,640
We're here for an interview.
Not to say goodbye.

648
00:45:41,640 --> 00:45:46,111
Joanne, just leave Joyce be.

649
00:45:46,111 --> 00:45:51,316
Joyce deserves a break
to find her peace of mind, madam.

650
00:45:51,316 --> 00:45:57,656
I never asked for your stupid opinions!

651
00:45:57,656 --> 00:45:59,524
Who made Joyce's career?

652
00:45:59,524 --> 00:46:01,193
Who gave up her whole life for your career?

653
00:46:01,193 --> 00:46:05,330
Mom, you can't talk to
Dad and Odet like that!

654
00:46:05,330 --> 00:46:08,199
If you're mad, take it out on me.

655
00:46:12,404 --> 00:46:13,538
There.

656
00:46:13,538 --> 00:46:15,473
I took it out on you.

657
00:46:16,575 --> 00:46:20,579
Now... proceed with your explanation.

658
00:46:20,579 --> 00:46:24,182
And stop with your drama.

659
00:46:25,817 --> 00:46:27,485
Continue.

660
00:46:28,253 --> 00:46:31,022
- Sit down.
- Mom, I don't want this anymore.

661
00:46:34,216 --> 00:46:37,585
How often do I have to say it?
I'm done with it.

662
00:46:39,865 --> 00:46:42,533
I want to rest, Mom.

663
00:46:44,002 --> 00:46:46,004
I want to breathe.

664
00:46:46,004 --> 00:46:47,673
I want to get lost.

665
00:46:47,673 --> 00:46:51,542
I want to get lost and find myself.

666
00:46:53,412 --> 00:46:56,581
You want to get lost?

667
00:46:56,581 --> 00:46:59,017
You want to get lost?

668
00:46:59,017 --> 00:47:00,919
You want to get lost?

669
00:47:00,919 --> 00:47:03,121
Fine! Get lost!

670
00:47:03,121 --> 00:47:04,089
- Mommy!
- That's enough!

671
00:47:04,089 --> 00:47:05,090
Mom...

672
00:47:05,090 --> 00:47:06,091
- Madam!
- Joanne!

673
00:47:06,091 --> 00:47:07,959
- Madam!
- What's happening?

674
00:47:21,807 --> 00:47:24,676
As you climb to the top,
it devours you more and more.

675
00:47:24,676 --> 00:47:26,578
It makes you more greedy.

676
00:47:26,578 --> 00:47:30,649
And whenever you use the typewriter,
there's always a price to pay.

677
00:47:30,649 --> 00:47:34,186
Your child with Joyce
disappears from this world.

678
00:47:34,186 --> 00:47:35,687
Isn't he having a heart attack?

679
00:47:35,687 --> 00:47:36,922
I'm begging...

680
00:47:36,922 --> 00:47:38,156
You should have stayed out of this, kid.

681
00:47:38,156 --> 00:47:41,092
All your visions are real.
